  <!-- Women in Alco-Bev -->
  <section id="revolution">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Industry Disruption</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Women Leading India's Alco-Bev Revolution</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        The Indian alco-bev sector is surging toward <strong>US $57.3 Billion by 2029</strong>. Women aren't merely driving luxury consumption—they are founding distilleries, designing master distillations, and steering market expansions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Luxury Rum Vanguard • Goa / Mumbai</div>
        <h3>Kasturi Banerjee</h3>
        <div class="role-title">Founder, Stilldistilling Spirits (Maka Zai)</div>
        <p>
          Transitioned seamlessly from a 16-year corporate banking career to artisan distilling. She shattered barriers by creating Maka Zai, proving that women are defining premium barrel aging, bespoke flavor notes, and sold-out luxury tiers.
        </p>
        <div class="quote-box">
          "Flavor profile mastery belongs to those who dare redefine palate expectations."
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Manufacturing Pioneer • India's 1st</div>
        <h3>Vaniitha Jaiin</h3>
        <div class="role-title">Revelry Distillery &amp; Vanaha Gin</div>
        <p>
          Recognized as India's first woman to own and construct a full-scale alco-bev distillery. Her visionary journey shifted the paradigm from marketing into industrial fermentation, grain-to-glass science, and heavy infrastructure.
        </p>
        <div class="quote-box">
          "Pioneered the transition from consumer-side marketing to hard-core factory distillation."
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Craft Gin Movement • Global Distillati
